<apex:component controller="EndorsementDocuments_Ctrl">
    <apex:stylesheet value="{!$Resource.PolicyDocumentsCSS}" />
    <apex:attribute name="recordIdParam" description="" type="String" assignTo="{!recordId}" />
    <p class="heading"> 
        Annual Aggregate Deductible Endorsement
    </p>
    <p class="normalParagraph">
        It is agreed that Item 8 of the Declarations is amended to read as follows:<br/>
        <table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width:100%">
            <tr>
                <td style="width:5%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                    <p class="normalParagraph">
                        <span class="normalBoldParagraph"> 8. </span>
                    </p>
                </td>
                <td style="width:35%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                    <p class="normalParagraph">
                        Deductible:
                    </p>
                </td>
                <td style="width:30%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                    <p class="normalParagraph">
                        Per Claim $<apex:outPutText value="{0,number,#,##0}" rendered="{!NOT(hasOneNonFinalQuote)}">
                        <apex:param value="{!endorsement.Policy__r.Per_Claim_Deductible_Amount__c}"/>
                        </apex:outPutText>  
                        <apex:outPutText value="{0,number,#,##0}" rendered="{!(hasOneNonFinalQuote)}">
                        <apex:param value="{!quote.Deductible__r.Deductible_Amount__c}"/>
                        </apex:outPutText>
                    </p>
                </td>
                <td style="width:30%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                    <p class="normalParagraph">
                        Aggregate $<apex:outPutText value="{0,number,#,##0}"  rendered="{!NOT(hasOneNonFinalQuote)}">
                        <apex:param value="{!endorsement.Policy__r.Per_Claim_Deductible_Amount__c}"/>
                        </apex:outPutText>
                        <apex:outPutText value="{0,number,#,##0}"  rendered="{!(hasOneNonFinalQuote)}">
                        <apex:param value="{!quote.Deductible__r.Deductible_Amount__c}"/>
                        </apex:outPutText>
                    </p>
                </td>
            </tr>
    </table>
    </p>
    <br/>
    <br/>
    <p class="normalParagraph">
        It is further agreed that<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> IV. LIMIT OF LIABILITY AND DEDUCTIBLE, E. </span>of this Policy is hereby deleted in its entirety and is replaced by the following:<br/>
        <span class="normalBoldParagraph"> IV. LIMIT OF LIABILITY AND DEDUCTIBLE </span>
    </p>
    <table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="width:95%" align="right">
        <tr>
            <td style="width:5%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                <p class="normalParagraph">
                    <span class="normalBoldParagraph"> E. </span>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="width:95%;" class="tableDataLeft">
                <p class="normalParagraph">
                    Subject to the Limit of Liability:<br/>
                    The<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>is liable to pay<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Damages </span>in excess of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>. The<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>is liable to pay<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Claim Expenses </span>up to $5,000 and in excess of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>. The<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>is the maximum amount the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured </span>will pay for<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Damages </span>and<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Claim Expenses </span>arising out all<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Claims </span>in a single<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Policy Period </span>. The<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Named Insured </span>is responsible for the payment of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>, and each<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured </span>is individually liable for the payment of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>. In the event that the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>expends funds for<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Damages </span>or<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Claim Expenses </span>on an<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured’s </span>behalf, the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured </span>will reimburse the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>for such expenditures up to the amount of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible. </span>  Reimbursement of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible </span>will be due within thirty (30) days of the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company’s </span>first demand or thirty (30) days from the date the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>or counsel appointed by the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>first bills the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured, </span>whichever is earlier. If the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured </span>does not reimburse the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>or counsel appointed by the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>within sixty (60) days, the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>will be entitled to recover from the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Insured </span>reasonable legal fees, costs, and expenses incurred by the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Company </span>in collecting the<span class="normalBoldParagraph"> Deductible. </span>
                </p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>
    <div style="clear:both;">
    </div>
    <br/>
    <br/>
    <p class="normalParagraph">
        All other terms, conditions, limitations and exclusions of the Policy to which this endorsement is attached remain unchanged.
    </p>
    <!-- <div style="width:30%;margin-top:160px;float:right">
        <c:AuthorisedSigntoryComponent ></c:AuthorisedSigntoryComponent>
    </div> -->
</apex:component>